  "material_conclusion": "Lagged transaction and active-address growth reduced some drawdown but failed to preserve Bitcoin participation. The primary earned 112.86900829% in Design versus buy-and-hold 129.60544229%, then only 71.58206970% in Validation versus 464.75475156%. Validation drawdown improved by just 3.81226381 percentage points, while upside capture was 15.402117% and Calmar was 2.51413044 versus buy-and-hold 14.39575015. The TxCnt-only neighbor nearly replicated passive exposure and return without improving Calmar enough to establish independent value; the AdrActCnt-only neighbor was identical to the failed primary in Validation. This is not a generalizable risk-adjusted alpha mechanism.",
